      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Since $f(x)=x$ is the solution for which $f(x)=f^{-1}(x)$, if we solve this equation, we can find the value of $x$. Starting with the equation $f(x)=x$, we know that $x=3x-8$ will make $f(x)=f^{-1}(x)$ true, giving us:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n3x-8 &= x \\\\\n&= 2x-8 \\\\\n&= 0 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow x &= \\boxed{4}\n\\end{align*}",
