      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given that $f(x)=3x-8$, finding the inverse of $f(x)$ would mean finding $f^{-1}(x)$ for $y=3x-8$. This inverse function can be expressed as:\n\\begin{align*} y &= 3x-8 \\\\ y+8 &= 3x \\\\ x &= \\frac{y+8}{3} \\end{align*}\nFor $f(x)$ with the inverse function $y=f^{-1}(x)$, this means our inverse function, $f^{-1}(x)$, is given by:\n$$ f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x+8}{3} $$\nWe want to solve $f(x)=f^{-1}(x)$. This leads to:\n\\begin{align*} 3x-8 &= \\frac{x+8}{3} \\\\ 9x-24 &= x+8 \\Rightarrow 9x-x &= 8+24 \\\\ 8x &= 32 \\Rightarrow x &= 4 \\end{align*}\nThus, our answer is $\\boxed{x=4}$. The value of $x$ for which $f(x)=f^{-1}(x)$ is \\boxed{4}.",
